  "notes": "USAGE:\nSense 1 (to master) takes a direct object with を: {技|わざ}を{極|きわ}める (to master a technique). Sense 2 (to reach the extreme) also uses を: {贅沢|ぜいたく}を{極|きわ}める (to reach the height of luxury). The pattern 〜を{極|きわ}める is characteristic and appears in literary and formal contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {道|みち}を{極|きわ}める: to master one's path/craft\n- {贅沢|ぜいたく}を{極|きわ}める: to reach the height of luxury\n- {混乱|こんらん}を{極|きわ}める: to be in utter chaos\n- {技|わざ}を{極|きわ}める: to perfect a technique\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {究|きわ}める: to investigate thoroughly (different kanji, focuses on research/inquiry)\n- {極|きわ}み: the extreme, the peak (noun form)",
